</p>\n","topic":{"id":1007,"name":"The Chain Rule With Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":728,"title":"Differentiating a General Exponential Function Using the Chain Rule"},"group":{"id":94967,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[{"id":null,"number":null,"answers":[]}],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14245004,"answer":{"id":62278747,"cread":"2026-10-15T15:22:52.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":14586},"graphic":false,"difficultyClass":"difficultyEasy","difficultySymbol":"E","rendered":true,"testMode":false}},{"id":62278761,"created":"2026-10-15T15:23:06.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9734,"number":2,"createdStr":"Thu, Oct 15th @ 3:23 PM","timeElapsedFormatted":"0:10","question":{"id":1953,"format":"MC","difficulty":1,"exampleId":729,"text":"<p>Find $f'(x)$ for $f(x) =e^{x^2}.$</p>\n","choice1":"$2xe^{x^2}$","choice2":"$xe^{x^2}$ ","choice3":"$e^{2x^2}$","choice4":"$2e^{x^2}$","choice5":"$x^2$","freeAnswerChoice":" ","explanation":"<p>First, we express $f(x)$ as the composite function\n\\[\nf = e^u, \\qquad u=x^2.\n\\]</p>\n<p>Differentiating gives\n\\[\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u} = e^u,\\qquad \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x} =2x.\n\\]</p>\n<p>We now apply the chain rule and get\n\\begin{align*}\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d x} &= \\dfrac{\\textrm d f}{\\textrm d u}\\cdot \\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d x}\\\\[5pt]\n&=e^u \\cdot (2x)\\\\[5pt]\n&=2xe^u\\\\[5pt]\n&=2xe^{x^2}.\n\\end{align*}</p>\n","topic":{"id":1007,"name":"The Chain Rule With Exponential Functions"},"example":{"id":729,"title":"Differentiating an Exponential Function with a Nonlinear Exponent"},"group":{"id":94989,"calculator":"None"},"graphics":[],"selects":[],"inputAnswers":[],"body":null,"taskId":14245004,"answer":{"id":62278761,"cread":"2026-10-15T15:23:06.000Z","choices":null,"correct":1,"selectedChoice":1,"freeResponse":null,"timeElapsed":9734},"graphi